---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const nunUrl = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/nun`.replace(/\/+/g, '/');
---

<Layout 
  title="About Echo Stories - Independent Film Production Prague"
  description="Prague-based independent film production company founded by Iuliia Mamaeva. We develop author-driven fiction and documentary films from Europe, Central Asia, and the Middle East."
  type="website"
  showFooter={false}
>
  <div class="editorial-shell py-12 md:py-20">
    <header class="editorial-rule mb-8 border-b pb-7 md:mb-12 md:pb-10">
      <h1 class="editorial-title font-serif">About</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.65fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-16">
    <div class="max-w-prose space-y-6 text-base leading-relaxed md:text-lg">
      <p>
        We are a Prague-based independent film production company founded by producer
        <strong>Iuliia Mamaeva</strong>, specializing in author-driven fiction and documentary films.
        We connect European talent with filmmakers from Central Asia and the Middle East,
        building a slate defined by international collaboration and cross-regional storytelling.
      </p>

      <p>
        Our mission is to amplify unique voices and untold stories from diverse cultural backgrounds,
        creating films that resonate across borders. We focus on creative, author-driven projects
        that challenge conventional narratives and offer fresh perspectives on contemporary issues.
      </p>
      
      <p>
        Although recently established, the company has quickly gained recognition in the international
        film community, participating in major development platforms including the
        <strong>MIDPOINT Series Launch/Short</strong>, <strong>Be2Be Exchange at MIA</strong>,
        <strong>East-West Talent Lab</strong>, and the <strong>ECAM Forum</strong>.
      </p>
      
      <p>
        Currently in development is the debut feature film of director Liza Chakanova,
        <em>"Kupala Night"</em>, which won the Belarusian Filmmakers' Network development incubator
        program and was presented at the <strong>Berlinale – BIFA Pitching Event 2026</strong>.
        The company's short animation <em>Nun (Jeptiška)</em> has been selected for
        <strong>Zlín Film Festival</strong>, <strong>Anifilm</strong>, <strong>StopTrik</strong>,
        <strong>CINANIMA</strong> and the <strong>London International Animation Festival</strong>,
        among others. It also took part in <strong>Cannes Short Film Corner | Rendez-vous Industry</strong>.
        The horror-comedy mockumentary series <em>"Paralegal"</em> was awarded the
        <strong>Writers' Vision Pitch Award</strong> at the <strong>Seriencamp Festival 2026</strong>,
        which particularly honors projects in an early creative phase.
      </p>
    </div>
    
    <aside class="editorial-rule border-t pt-7 lg:border-l lg:border-t-0 lg:pl-8 lg:pt-0" aria-labelledby="selected-projects">
      <h2 id="selected-projects" class="mb-6 font-serif text-3xl">Selected Projects</h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-base">
        <div>
          <p class="editorial-label mb-1">Completed</p>
          <a href={`${nunUrl}#festivals`} class="text-gray-700 underline underline-offset-4 dark:text-gray-300">Nun (Jeptiška) — festival selections and industry showcase</a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="editorial-label mb-1">Post-production</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">Night Games (short), The Apple Tree That Blossomed Twice (short)</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="editorial-label mb-1">In development</p>
          <ul class="space-y-1 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <li>Kupala Night (feature)</li>
            <li>
              Paralegal (horror-comedy mockumentary series)
              <div class="mb-2 mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"><span aria-hidden="true">🏆</span> Writers' Vision Pitch Award · Seriencamp Festival 2026</div>
            </li>
            <li>Ai-Ai (3D animated series)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
